From: OHOS wine port
Subject: [PATCH] vkd3d: fix incompatible pointer type in swapchain helper

The device10 patch retyped d3d12_device::ID3D12Device_iface to
ID3D12Device10, while d3d12_swapchain_device_iface() still declares an
ID3D12Device9* result. GCC accepted the implicit COM-interface
downcast with a warning; current clang treats
-Wincompatible-pointer-types as an error in C and aborts the build.
Add an explicit cast (the interface layouts are compatible, the
underlying object is the same d3d12_device).
---
 libs/vkd3d/swapchain.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libs/vkd3d/swapchain.c b/libs/vkd3d/swapchain.c
--- a/libs/vkd3d/swapchain.c
+++ b/libs/vkd3d/swapchain.c
@@ -230,7 +230,7 @@ static inline const struct vkd3d_vk_device_procs* d3d12_swapchain_procs(struct d
 
 static inline struct ID3D12Device9* d3d12_swapchain_device_iface(struct d3d12_swapchain* swapchain)
 {
-    return &swapchain->command_queue->device->ID3D12Device_iface;
+    return (struct ID3D12Device9*)&swapchain->command_queue->device->ID3D12Device_iface;
 }
 
 static inline struct d3d12_device* d3d12_swapchain_device(struct d3d12_swapchain* swapchain)
-- 
2.34.1
